            text: "Tekton, in most cases. Its large sets cost less per tool, the organisers and racks are well thought out, and the lifetime warranty is claimed directly with no receipt — which suits someone building a first set rather than replacing individual tools. GearWrench makes more sense once you know which specific tools you use most and want the ratcheting versions of them.",
