          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Both appear in professional boxes, usually alongside premium brands. GearWrench has deeper penetration in automotive shops because of its ratcheting wrench range and its availability through parts stores and industrial distributors. Tekton is more common among independent technicians and serious home mechanics who buy direct and value the price-to-quality ratio.",
