    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 lg:py-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">

        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic border-l-4 border-[#38BDF8] pl-6 bg-gray-50 py-4 rounded-r-xl">
          The short version: buy Tekton for the bulk of a hand tool collection and GearWrench for anything that ratchets. Both brands make good tools at fair prices, and the interesting differences are in business model and specialism rather than in raw material quality.
        </p>

        <h2 id="who-they-are" class="scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
          1. Who Each Brand Actually Is
        </h2>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Tekton</h3>
        <p>
          Tekton is a direct-to-consumer brand headquartered in Grand Rapids, Michigan. It engineers, specifies and inspects in the United States, manufactures primarily in Taiwan and China, and sells almost entirely through its own website and Amazon. That last point is the whole commercial story: by removing the distributor, the retailer and the tool truck franchisee from the chain — each of whom typically adds a substantial markup — it can put comparable steel in your hand for meaningfully less money.
        </p>
        <p>
          The company spent its first years selling a mixed bag of imported tools and has spent the decade since systematically upgrading its lines. Its reputation now rests on two things: a very strong price-to-quality ratio in core hand tools, and a lifetime warranty that is unusually painless to use. Our full <a href="/tekton-tools-review/">Tekton tools review</a> covers the range in depth.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">GearWrench</h3>
        <p>
          GearWrench is a professional-oriented brand within the Apex Tool Group, and its identity is built on one invention: the ratcheting combination wrench. When it launched that tool in the 1990s it created a category that every other brand now copies, and the ratcheting mechanism remains the thing GearWrench does better than almost anyone at its price.
        </p>
        <p>
          Distribution is conventional and broad — auto parts stores, industrial supply houses, big-box retailers, online sellers — which means a GearWrench tool is usually available today, locally, in a way a Tekton tool is not. Like Tekton, it manufactures largely in Asia to its own specifications. The two brands are far closer in metallurgy than their different market positioning suggests.
        </p>

        <!-- Head-to-Head Comparison Table -->
        <div class="my-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-950 to-gray-900 rounded-3xl p-8 lg:p-12 text-white shadow-2xl">
          <h2 id="head-to-head" class="scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black text-white mt-0 mb-8 border-none text-center">Head-to-Head Comparison</h2>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-gray-700">
                  <th class="py-3 px-4 text-[#38BDF8] font-bold text-base">Category</th>
